From: Marcelo Alcantara <maralc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] apple: keep the console silent on Macs

Omarchy boots the Mac to a splash, not a terminal: with CONFIG_SILENT_CONSOLE
the console is muted whenever the 'silent' variable is set, so the default
environment sets it. Only U-Boot is silenced (CONFIG_SILENT_U_BOOT_ONLY);
the kernel command line is untouched.
---
 board/apple/mac/mac.env | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/board/apple/mac/mac.env b/board/apple/mac/mac.env
--- a/board/apple/mac/mac.env
+++ b/board/apple/mac/mac.env
@@ -2,3 +2,4 @@ stdin=serial,usbkbd,spikbd,mtpkbd
 stdout=vidconsole,serial
 stderr=vidconsole,serial
 boot_targets=nvme usb
+silent=1

The banner "U-Boot 2026.07 ..." is announced on the video console after
relocation through console_puts_select(), which never looks at the silent
flag; a silent console stays silent for the banner too.
---
 common/console.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/common/console.c b/common/console.c
--- a/common/console.c
+++ b/common/console.c
@@ -1022,6 +1022,9 @@ int console_announce_r(void)
 #if !CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(PRE_CONSOLE_BUFFER)
 	char buf[DISPLAY_OPTIONS_BANNER_LENGTH];
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SILENT_CONSOLE) && (gd->flags & GD_FLG_SILENT))
+		return 0;
+
 	display_options_get_banner(false, buf, sizeof(buf));
 
 	console_puts_select(stdout, false, buf);
